{
  "scenario": "A small part of the grid model of Northgrid, a fictional transmission system operator, as merged from the CGMES equipment, topology, steady state hypothesis, state variables, short circuit and geographical location profiles. An 85 km 400 kV line runs from Brookfield power station, where a 650 MVA generator feeds the grid through a 21/400 kV step-up transformer, to Ashby substation, where a 400/220 kV autotransformer with an on-load tap changer supplies a 220 kV load. The data has the substations, voltage levels, busbars, breakers, terminals, connectivity and topological nodes, current limits on the line, and the power flow solution: bus voltages and the flows at each terminal.",
